('CIT_TERROR_THEOG','ENT_TERROR','SRC_HESIOD_THEOGONY','Hesiod, Theogony','lines 933-937','Also Cytherea bare to Ares the shield-piercer Panic and Fear, terrible gods who drive in disorder the close ranks of men in numbing war, with the help of Ares, sacker of towns: and Harmonia whom high-spirited Cadmus made his wife.','Hugh G. Evelyn-White',1914,'https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/348','primary-verbatim',NULL,DATE '2026-06-17','deterministic verbatim extraction + substring gate (Gutenberg #348, line-numbered)',1),
